; FileCheck spec for param_attrs_freeze_interior.logos — the interior-mutability
; POPULATION, asked of the compiler.
;
; EVERY LINE HERE MUST SHOW THE ABSENCE OF `noalias` AND `readonly`. Each is
; pinned as a literal, whole parameter list in the param_attrs_freeze idiom: the
; `{{[^(]*}}` wildcards cannot cross a `(`, so an attribute appearing where it
; must not is exactly as red as one vanishing where it must be. That two-
; directionality is the whole point — the failure mode being guarded against is
; an attribute APPEARING.
;
; ⚠ `; AXIS <id>` markers are machine-read: tests/logos/shared_ref_ub_lint.sh
; requires every ledger row that claims an axis to have one here, and every
; marker here to be claimed by a ledger row. A ledger row cannot quietly stop
; being checked against the artifact.
;
; LAYOUTS, HAND-DERIVED (all confirmed against the emitted IR afterwards):
;   Cell<i64>        {UnsafeCell<i64>}                            =  8/8
;   RefCell<i64>     {UnsafeCell<i32>, UnsafeCell<i64>}           = 16/8
;                    (4 + 4 pad + 8; align 8 from the i64)
;   OnceCell<i64>    {UnsafeCell<i64>, UnsafeCell<bool>}          = 16/8
;                    (8 + 1, tail-padded to align 8)
;   UnsafeCell<i64>  #[repr(transparent)] over i64                =  8/8
;   LazyCell<i64>    {OnceCell<i64>, fn() -> i64}                 = 24/8
;   AtomicI64        {UnsafeCell<i64>}                            =  8/8
;   Writ             {UnsafeCell<Allocator>, UnsafeCell<i64>}     = 32/8
;                    (Allocator = {*mut Segment, *mut Segment, i64} = 24/8)
;   Mutex<i64>       {UnsafeCell<i64>, *mut u8}                   = 16/8
;   RwLock<i64>      {UnsafeCell<i64>, *mut u8}                   = 16/8

; ── THE CELL FAMILY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; AXIS axis_cell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_cell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)
; AXIS axis_refcell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_refcell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_oncecell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_oncecell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_unsafecell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_unsafecell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── THE TRANSITIVE LAYER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
; LazyCell has NO UnsafeCell of its own. It is non-Freeze only because the
; recursion descends into its OnceCell field. This line is the one that catches
; a field recursion that stops one level too early — which is the same failure
; shape as the tuple arm that was MEASURED to hand out a wrong noalias.
; AXIS axis_lazycell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_lazycell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(24) %0)

; ── ONE REPRESENTATIVE ATOMIC ──────────────────────────────────────────────
; The clause that silently went false last time was about the atomics; the other
; eleven are ledger rows, deliberately marked `-` rather than assumed covered.
; AXIS axis_atomic_i64
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_atomic_i64{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── THE NAMED LOAD-BEARING TYPES ───────────────────────────────────────────
; `Writ` is the live one: 367 `&Writ`/`&mut Writ` parameter occurrences in
; stdlib, every one of which would be told to LLVM as never-written if the arena
; and root ever lost their UnsafeCell wrappers.
; AXIS axis_writ
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_writ{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(32) %0)
;
; Mutex and RwLock have NO `&T` call site in the tree today — every method takes
; `self: *mut Mutex<T>`. These two lines are the standing gate for the day one
; appears. Note the layouts: stripping `UnsafeCell` off `data` leaves
; `{ i64, *mut u8 }`, still 16/8, so the SIZE does not move and only the aliasing
; pair does — a clean one-variable axis for exactly the edit that was measured to
; leave the old census exiting 0.
; AXIS axis_mutex
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_mutex{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_rwlock
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_rwlock{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
